    ("Where are the strongest winds of a typhoon?", "in the eyewall, around the eye", ["in the eye", "far outside the rain bands", "only on land"], "The eyewall has the strongest winds and heaviest rain."),
    ("Why does a typhoon weaken when it moves over land?", "it loses its supply of warm, moist air from the ocean", ["land makes the wind stronger", "mountains add more water", "the Sun stops shining"], "Typhoons get their energy from warm ocean water."),
    ("What does Tropical Cyclone Wind Signal No. 1 mean?", "strong winds are expected within 36 hours", ["the typhoon has already passed", "the strongest winds are expected within 12 hours", "there is no danger at all"], "Higher signal numbers mean stronger winds coming sooner."),
    ("Which Tropical Cyclone Wind Signal is the highest?", "Signal No. 5", ["Signal No. 1", "Signal No. 3", "Signal No. 10"], "PAGASA uses Signals No. 1 to No. 5."),
    ("What is a storm surge?", "an abnormal rise of sea water pushed onto land by a typhoon's winds", ["a strong earthquake", "a heavy rainfall on mountains", "a wave made by a ship"], "Storm surges can flood coastal areas, as in Typhoon Yolanda (Haiyan) in 2013."),
    ("Why should families near rivers evacuate during a strong typhoon?", "heavy rain can cause floods and flash floods", ["rivers dry up during typhoons", "typhoons make rivers freeze", "rivers attract lightning only"], "Heavy rain raises river levels quickly."),
    ("Which item should be in an emergency go bag?", "a flashlight, water, food, medicine and a radio", ["only toys and games", "a television", "a heavy cabinet"], "A go bag helps a family survive the first days after a disaster."),
    ("Why are many typhoons given local names by PAGASA?", "so that people can easily identify and remember each storm", ["to make them stronger", "to tell their exact speed", "because each one has a different eye"], "Local names help people follow warnings."),
    ("About how many tropical cyclones enter the Philippine Area of Responsibility each year?", "about 20", ["about 2", "about 100", "none"], "The Philippines is one of the most typhoon-prone countries."),
    ("What is a low pressure area (LPA)?", "a region where air pressure is lower than around it, which may develop into a tropical cyclone", ["a place with very cold air", "a region with no wind", "an area of high mountains"], "Air rises in an LPA and clouds form."),
    ("Which is the correct order as a storm grows stronger?", "tropical depression → tropical storm → severe tropical storm → typhoon → super typhoon", ["typhoon → tropical storm → tropical depression", "super typhoon → typhoon → tropical depression", "tropical storm → tropical depression → typhoon"], "PAGASA classifies tropical cyclones by wind speed."),
    ("Why do typhoons in the Philippines spin counterclockwise?", "because of the Earth's rotation in the Northern Hemisphere", ["because of the Moon", "because the wind comes from mountains", "because of ocean tides"], "The Coriolis effect makes storms spin counterclockwise north of the equator."),
    ("What should you do when a typhoon is near?", "stay indoors, away from windows, and listen to official warnings", ["go swimming at the beach", "climb a tall tree", "stand under a power line"], "Flying debris and floods are the main dangers."),
    ("Why do landslides often happen during typhoons?", "heavy rain soaks the soil on slopes, making it heavy and loose", ["the wind lifts the mountains", "typhoons make the ground freeze", "the Sun dries the soil quickly"], "Trees and roots help hold soil and reduce landslides."),
    ("Which months bring the most typhoons to the Philippines?", "June to November", ["January to March", "only December", "April only"], "Most typhoons come during the wet (rainy) season."),
    ("What happens to the air pressure as a typhoon comes closer?", "it drops", ["it rises", "it stays the same", "it becomes zero"], "A barometer shows falling pressure when a storm is near."),
    ("Which instrument measures wind speed?", "an anemometer", ["a barometer", "a rain gauge", "a thermometer"], "Its cups spin faster in stronger wind."),
    ("Which instrument shows the direction the wind is coming from?", "a wind vane", ["a rain gauge", "a thermometer", "a barometer"], "The arrow points to where the wind is coming from."),
