    ("What is the epicenter of an earthquake?", "the point on the Earth's surface directly above the focus", ["the deepest point of the Earth", "the center of the Earth", "a place far from the earthquake"], "Shaking is usually strongest near the epicenter."),
    ("Which agency gives earthquake information in the Philippines?", "PHIVOLCS", ["PAGASA", "DENR", "DOTr"], "PHIVOLCS reports magnitude and intensity."),
    ("What does the magnitude of an earthquake measure?", "the energy released at the source", ["the damage in one town", "how long people felt it", "the number of buildings"], "Each earthquake has one magnitude."),
    ("What does the intensity of an earthquake describe?", "how strongly it is felt and the damage it causes at a place", ["the energy at the focus", "the depth of the focus", "the length of the fault"], "Intensity is different in different places; PHIVOLCS uses intensities I to X."),
    ("What should you do during an earthquake?", "Duck, Cover and Hold", ["run outside while the ground is shaking", "stand near glass windows", "use the elevator"], "Drop down, cover your head under a sturdy table and hold on."),
