TIDES = [
    ("What causes tides?", "mainly the pull of the Moon's gravity on the oceans", ["the wind", "earthquakes", "the rotation of the Sun"], "The Sun's gravity also affects tides."),
    ("How many high tides does a coast usually have each day?", "two", ["one", "four", "none"], "There are usually two high tides and two low tides each day."),
    ("What is a high tide?", "when the sea level is highest along the shore", ["when the sea water is coldest", "when the waves are smallest", "when the Moon is not in the sky"], "At high tide water comes farther up the beach."),
    ("What is a low tide?", "when the sea level is lowest along the shore", ["when the sea is warmest", "when the Moon is closest", "when there are no waves at all"], "At low tide more of the beach can be seen."),
    ("What is a spring tide?", "a tide with the highest high tides and lowest low tides, at new moon and full moon", ["a tide that happens only in the spring season", "a very small tide at quarter moon", "a tide caused by rain"], "The Sun and Moon are in line, so their pulls add up."),
    ("What is a neap tide?", "a tide with the smallest difference between high and low tide, at the quarter moons", ["the highest tide of the year", "a tide caused by a typhoon", "a tide only in rivers"], "The Sun and Moon pull at right angles."),
    ("Why does the Moon affect tides more than the Sun?", "the Moon is much closer to the Earth", ["the Moon is bigger than the Sun", "the Moon is hotter", "the Sun has no gravity"], "Distance matters a lot for tides."),
    ("Why do fishers in coastal villages check the tide?", "tides affect when boats can leave and where fish and shellfish can be found", ["tides tell the time of earthquakes", "tides show the color of the sea", "tides decide the weather"], "Many people gather shellfish at low tide."),
    ("About how long is it from one high tide to the next?", "about 12 hours and 25 minutes", ["exactly 24 hours", "about 1 hour", "about one week"], "Tides come about 50 minutes later each day."),
    ("What happens to the sea level at the moment of a full moon?", "it has bigger tides (spring tides)", ["there are no tides", "it freezes", "the tide stops for a day"], "The Sun, Earth and Moon are in a line."),
    ("Which is a benefit of tides?", "they can be used to make electricity (tidal energy)", ["they stop typhoons", "they make the sea fresh water", "they cause day and night"], "Moving water can turn turbines."),
    ("Which statement about tides is correct?", "the oceans bulge on the side facing the Moon and on the opposite side", ["only the side facing the Moon has high tide", "the oceans do not move", "the Moon pushes water away"], "That is why there are two high tides a day."),
    ("Mangrove areas are flooded at high tide and exposed at low tide. Why are mangroves important?", "they protect coasts from waves and storm surges and are nurseries for fish", ["they cause tides", "they make the sea salty", "they block sunlight from the sea"], "Mangrove roots trap mud and break waves."),
    ("Why is it dangerous to walk far out on a beach at low tide?", "the tide may come back quickly and cut you off", ["the sand becomes hot", "the Moon may fall", "the sea becomes fresh water"], "Always check tide times."),
    ("What is the tidal range?", "the difference in height between high tide and low tide", ["the length of a beach", "the speed of the waves", "the depth of the sea"], "The tidal range is largest at spring tides."),
    ("Which Moon phases bring neap tides?", "first quarter and last quarter", ["new moon and full moon", "only full moon", "only new moon"], "The Sun and Moon pull at right angles."),
]

